{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01VokF6KTjCnk9DA6wrgVQSD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user productivity and R&D mission-control system. Grounded summary of what it IS:\n\n**Purpose**\n- A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that turns plain-text markdown files into a live, interactive dashboard â€” markdown is the single source of truth (no database, no lock files).\n- Everything lives in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`); no OneDrive, no siblings, no syncing.\n\n**What it does (core task manager)**\n- Manages a task lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored) across domain files (academic, commercial, family, writing) plus a dashboard, projects list, and quick-capture inbox.\n- Provides both a browser GUI and a mirrored CLI (`anchor.py`) for the same operations (done/add/capture/cancel/save/restore), and regenerates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n**What it ships (the application + runtime)**\n- `anchor_gui.py` â€” a self-contained Python **stdlib-only** HTTP server (no external deps, one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals) that generates the full dashboard HTML and writes directly to the markdown files.\n- Runs **persistently** as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777` (you don't launch it by hand).\n- A daily 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that parses every file, exercises every endpoint, walks a synthetic task through all states, and writes dated health reports â€” fully stubbed (never live `claude`).\n\n**The bigger thing it has grown into â€” an R&D \"cockpit\"**\n- Beyond tasks, Anchor is a **mission-control for trio-driven R&D** (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Each project gets a window where each lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build) shows its most-recent session as a tile with one honest status light (green/amber/red/grey).\n- Clicking a tile expands an **inline panel in place** (never a new page): a cached, validated summary on top and a real, resizable **ConPTY terminal** (xterm.js over WebSocket/SSE) below. Opening a session feels like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session â€” the lane's skill auto-loads **once**, greets **once**, no repeating-prompt loop.\n- Ships durable session machinery: per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, cached project/session summaries, stage handoffs, deliverable launch-by-type, cost/tokens/time rollups, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), and a grass-idea board.\n- This has been built incrementally through four design generations (v1 â†’ v2 \"sessions/summaries\" â†’ v3 \"Mission Control\" â†’ v4 \"Project Cockpit\", currently merged to master). It's branded as a Ghost World Labs tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\".\n\nOne honest caveat: these claims are grounded in the project's own docs (CLAUDE.md, the locked North Stars) rather than re-verified against the live running code â€” they describe what the project is documented to be and ship."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24709,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24709},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e25a118-4fd0-44e0-b81e-5ed79a219108","uuid":"9e1bc735-f1f2-4aac-b57a-f2f7675c8462","request_id":"req_011Cc1eeyo9iJuhbZwmLkuNe"}
